WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.850
Abraham: Reporting cyber security
incidents is important in

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:07.260
maintaining the resilience of
public communications networks and

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:09.109
understanding the threat environment.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:13.610
This enables companies and organisations
to strengthen their procedures and

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.849
put contingencies into place by
learning from other’s mistakes and

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.369
keeping up to date with trends.

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.780
Nicole: Staff need to be made aware
of the importance of cyber security

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.899
as they represent the business and
are often handling sensitive data.

00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:31.740
Companies should make sure that all
staff are fully aware of issues and

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:36.400
what steps to take to maintain security
and what to do in case of a breach.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:39.420
This training should be
delivered in a regular cadence

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.519
to ensure staff are always aware.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.370
Abraham: A cyber security issue
usually means that something

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.760
has, or could have, put critical
systems or sensitive data at risk.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.309
It can be anything from a malware attack
to an employee clicking on an email or

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:58.220
link from an untrusted source or losing
a storage device with sensitive data.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.350
Nicole: It maybe something as small
as someone putting their password on a

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.490
'post it' by their computer or sharing
their log in details with others.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.430
This might seem trivial and not a
'reportable offence' but it should be

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:16.390
addressed as it could lead to a potential
security risk with serious ramifications.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.310
It may cause loss of trust
in a company and financial

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.039
loss with legal implications.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:26.230
Abraham: There are many kinds of cyber
security incidents but those that

00:01:26.309 --> 00:01:30.560
involve personal data breaches need
to be reported to the ICO [Information

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.740
Commissioner’s Office] within 72
hours of becoming aware of it.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.390
If this affects an individual’s
rights and freedoms, then they

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:39.100
must also be told without delay.

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.550
Nicole: Where appropriate this will be
shared with the National Cyber security

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:49.880
centre [NCSC] and other law enforcement
and cyber crime agencies or regulators

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:55.460
such as NCA National Crime Agency,
the Financial Conduct Authority [FCA],

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.360
and the Payment Cards Industry [PCI].

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.730
Abraham: A key principle of the UK
General Data protection regulation

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:06.559
is that personal data is processed
securely and means that all systems

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:10.180
and services should have the correct
security to maintain confidentiality.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:14.960
Nicole: In some more exceptional
cases, a cyber security incident

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:17.299
can result in actual physical harm.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.489
This is especially true when it comes
to cyber-attacks on the healthcare

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.320
industry such as those affecting the NHS.

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:29.350
Also, with a wide range of new smart
appliances being developed especially

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:33.359
for the home including security
systems there is an opportunity

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.909
for hackers to take over personal
devices to surveil or gain control of.

00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:43.399
The rise of IOT devices has created
new problems with technology being

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.760
used in more day-to-day things meaning
that there are new risks emerging.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.620
Abraham: Vulnerability to cyber attack
should never be underestimated and hidden.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.320
It is important to remember that
thinking that 'you won't be hacked

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.640
because nobody would want to', is not a
good defence and is sometimes referred

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.810
to as 'security through obscurity'.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.679
To be able to maintain cyber security
at all levels it is important that

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:12.053
any issues, breaches, or attacks are
reported immediately to assess and

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.610
minimise any current or future damage.

